   "text": "The drawing shows an MMAE (monomethyl auristatin E) payload attached through a self-immolative p-aminobenzyl carbamate linker (PAB-Val-Ala) to a 6-aminohexanoyl spacer. The spacer ends in a methyl (Z)-maleamate (methyl ester of a cis-butenedioic acid monoamide).\n\nReading left to right:\n- **Maleamate cap:** a methyl ester on a cis C=C, followed by an amide NH.\n- **Spacer:** five CH2 groups and a carbonyl (the 6-aminohexanoyl unit), then an amide to valine.\n- **Dipeptide and PAB:** Val, then Ala, then an anilide on a para-substituted benzene whose CH2\u2013O\u2013C(=O) forms the carbamate.\n- **Auristatin core:** N-methyl-valine, valine, N-methyl-dolaisoleuine (with its OMe), dolaproine (pyrrolidine with its OMe and methyl), and a norephedrine-type amino alcohol bearing a phenyl ring.\n\nI assumed L-Val and L-Ala. For the auristatin stereocentres I took the configuration from the known MMAE SMILES, re-expressing each centre for my atom ordering, and checked each against the drawn wedges. The norephedrine centres follow MMAE as well.\n\nSMILES: COC(=O)/C=C\\C(=O)NCCCCCC(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)C(=O)Nc1ccc(COC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H]([C@@H](C)CC)[C@H](OC)CC(=O)N2CCC[C@H]2[C@H](OC)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C)[C@H](O)c2ccccc2)cc1"
  }
